  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Past habits",
     "texto": [
      "**Locuiam** means «I lived or used to live»; **eram**, «I was». We also use the imperfect to set the scene in a story.",
      "For a finished experience you have already seen the compound past: **am fost** («I was»). Do not confuse **eram** («I was») with **am fost** («I was» or «I have been»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Endings",
     "texto": [
      "In many verbs, the endings **-am, -ai, -a** help form the imperfect: **locuiam** (I/we used to live), **locuiai** (you used to live), **locuia** (he/she used to live). With **a fi** we use **eram, erai, era**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
